Design experiments for spec/incr.md's update rules (M7). Not part of any
gate; run by hand. Reviewer scripts copied here are adaptations; the
reviewers' own directories (.build/review-in72, .build/review-in77) stay
read-only.

edits.sh          WP-202: real edits to protoc's strutil.cc, objects only, classified by elfdiff.py.
elfdiff.py        WP-202: classify an object edit by WP-064a §3's refused-edit list; per-object census.
model_region.py   WP-207: IN-72 item 2's region rule (keep / grow in place / first fit / overflow region) over
                  the R-L reviewer's protoc builds; moved-definition counts beside WP-202's rule. From
                  review-in72/model_in72.py.
model_extract.py  WP-207: IN-71b's incremental archive extraction (KEY_REFS + ROUND, decremental repair,
                  forward addition) against resolve.md §4.1's closure from scratch; R1a, R1b, random hops.
crash_model.py    WP-207: IN-77's write protocol under kill / power loss at every step, with mtime and
                  fsync modelled; variants copy, in place, epoch mtime, rename-aside, boot id. From
                  review-in77/crash_model.py.
fsprobe.py        WP-207: does a write after utime(0) bump mtime; cost of the lock round trip.
bsprobe.sh        WP-207: do make and ninja relink after a torn output that is fresh, epoch-dated or missing.
symfill.py        WP-207: rebuild a linked file's .symtab the way IN-49a's update does, with or without fillers.
fillers.sh        WP-207: IN-49a's filler form against ~35 tools on AArch64, x86-64, i386 (uses symfill.py
                  and the prebuilt mortar). From review-in72/r7-fillers.sh.
fillcmp.py        WP-207: for the listing tools fillers.sh reports as differing, compare again without the filler
                  lines, index columns and the table-size lines (run: fillcmp.py SCRATCH/fill-T SECTION1-NAME).
extract_amended.py WP-211: R-2's extract_mine.py (.build/review-wp207, imported read-only by path) in the reading
                  WP-211's IN-71b leaves ("member", extracted or not), rounds judged by the support property.
crash_model.py    (WP-211) variants inplace-aside-link, -link-foreign, -rename-foreign: W4 as link + unlink,
                  each durable after its own directory fsync; a foreign output created at P inside the window.
